  "term": "anticholinergic effects",
  "definition": "Anticholinergic effects are changes caused by blocking acetylcholine at muscarinic receptors, which reduces parasympathetic nerve stimulation. In the eye, these effects can produce pupil dilation and temporary paralysis of focusing.",
